https://sourceforge.net/apps/trac/sourceforge/newticket

> [...] ... all
> are effects that are nearly completely negated by having a unicorn
> horn - thus the game gets simpler as it goes on, and I think that's
> the wrong way for it to be. [...]

This is a long-standing criticism of NetHack that it gets easier along
the way and that you're practically ascended if you're past the
castle (at least for serial ascenders).

For a beginner there's the fear that something bad happens on the
ascension run and the relief when nothing does (although rarely
something does happen :-) is part of what NetHack makes memorable.


Interestingly even though I don't consider UnNetHack really harder
(minus some exploitable stuff and Elbereth not working on some unique
monsters) there have been some deaths on the public server on the
ascension run on the planes:
http://un.nethack.nu/user/sp3ctum/dumps/sp3ctum.1298583233.txt.html
http://un.nethack.nu/user/blister/dumps/blister.1301505445.txt.html

I'm not entirely sure I can blame it only on the players but I
wouldn't know what I've changed that would cause this.

